  "application_type_full": "Prior Approval: New dwellinghouses on terrace buildings in commercial or mixed use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\rLocation Plan - D00 Rev. A\rProposed Block Plan - D09 Rev. F\rProposed Third Floor Plan - D01 Rev. G\rProposed Streetscene Plan - D50 Rev. D\rProposed Site Levels Plan - D07\rProposed Roof Plan - D31\r\rOther documents submitted with the application:\rExternal Living Wall Outline Specification\rParking Design Management Plan\rUnilateral Undertaking\rDaylight and Sunlight Assessment\rPlanning Statement\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of the required long-stay/short-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThese details should demonstrate:\r\rLocation: Near entrances or main access\rDesign: Stands\rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit\rCoverage: Covered\rAccessibility: Step-free, no obstructions\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024), shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The glazing serving the third floor rear windows of the development indicated on drawing D50 Rev. D shall be in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 3 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority.\r \rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r",
    "No piling shall take place until a piling method statement (detailing the depth and type of piling to be undertaken and the methodology by which such piling will be carried out, including measures to prevent and minimise the potential for damage to subsurface water infrastructure, and the programme for the works) and piling layout plan including all Thames Water clean water assets, the local topography and clearance between the face of the pile to the face of a pipe has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority in consultation with Thames Water. Any piling must be undertaken in accordance with the terms of the approved piling method statement and piling layout plan. \r\rReason: The proposed works will be in close proximity to underground water utility infrastructure. Piling has the potential to impact on local underground water utility infrastructure.\r",
    "No piling shall take place until a PILING METHOD STATEMENT (detailing the depth and type of piling to be undertaken and the methodology by which such piling will be carried out, including measures to prevent and minimise the potential for damage to subsurface sewerage infrastructure, and the programme for the works) and piling layout plan including all Thames Water wastewater assets, the local topography and clearance between the face of the pile to the face of a pipe has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority in consultation with Thames Water. Any piling must be undertaken in accordance with the terms of the approved piling method statement and piling layout plan. \r\rReason: The proposed works will be in close proximity to underground sewerage utility infrastructure. Piling has the potential to significantly impact / cause failure of local underground sewerage utility infrastructure.\r"
  ],
